From fa03f9b51ce5f77311e12276e744471980d86eba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuk3s <44327449+nuk3s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:47:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kv-offload): limit the overrun mark to the cold retry

Upstream base: the patch applies to local-inference-lab/vllm at
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the 702 patches of
spark-ds41f-1120 (candidate-62, 0001 to 0829) and patches 9030 to 9043
of this series.

Rationale: request_finished removed the overrun mark of 9043, but when a
request ended while its load was in flight, request_finished ran before
the failed load reached the connector. The mark then stayed until the
engine restarted, one entry for each such request. A mark that lasted
until the finish also made every later preemption of the request a full
recompute while the tier still held the blocks, and the two sets of the
disk backend kept one entry for each abandoned event for the life of
the process. With this patch the scheduler marks a request whose load
overran only while the request still waits for its retry, and ends the
mark when the cold retry is admitted, which is the call to
update_state_after_alloc with no external tokens. A request that
finished while the load was in flight, through an abort, an error,
kv_load_failure_policy "fail", or a reset, gets no mark, and after the
cold retry is admitted a preemption may load from the tier again. The
disk backend drops the abandon mark and the failure mark of an
abandoned event once the IO thread is done with the event. The log line
of the scheduler for an overrun now names a cache miss rather than a
recompute, because under the policy "fail" the request ends with an
error.

Quality implications: the patch does not change outputs. On a path that
stays slow, each preemption after the cold retry may overrun again and
costs one more bound.

Tests: on the CPU path the offload suite passed 219 tests, with 2
CUDA-only modules skipped, and 14 of those tests are new. A new file,
test_ds41_tier_overrun_core.py, runs the core scheduler with three
simulated ranks through an abort after the first report, an abort
before any report, five overruns under the policy "fail", a retry that
computes the whole prompt with no second load, and a preemption after
the cold retry that hits the tier again. The scheduler tests cover a
finish during the load and after a reset, two requests in one overrun
event, a retry with a local prefix, and the end of the mark at the
admission. The worker tests check that each rank reports each overrun
load once, that the overrun event is in the metadata of the same step,
and that the backend holds no mark after two overruns. A further test
checks that a degraded tier selects no store. Two timing tests no
longer depend on a margin of the host scheduler: the steady-load test
has a timeout of ten reads, and the drain test runs on a test clock with
gated copies. The CUDA path of an overrun was not tested, and no load
overran during the hardware run.

Upstream status: the patch is proposed to spark-ds41f in
experiments/2026-11-22-kv-disk-tier and has not been submitted to
local-inference-lab/vllm.
